# Shell / sandbox

When running any of these, always use Shell with `required_permissions: ["all"]`
(do not rely on the default sandbox):

- `./scripts/test.sh`
- `./scripts/dev-start.sh`
- `./scripts/dev-stop.sh`
- `./scripts/install-dependency.sh`

Reason:

- `test.sh` / `dev-*.sh`: process signals (kill) and/or writes under `/Volumes`
- `install-dependency.sh`: Playwright browsers install into `~/Library/Caches/ms-playwright`
  (scripts unset `PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH` so the Agent-injected sandbox cache is not used).
  A sandboxed shell cannot create the lock/cache dirs there → `EPERM`.

`format.sh` and `build.sh` may stay sandboxed.

Never run bare `npx playwright install` / `npm run test:e2e` — use the scripts above
(with `required_permissions: ["all"]`).
